Package: InfoMergeCluster
Type: Package
Title: Clustering of Sparse Longitudinal Data with Automatic Choice of the Number of Clusters
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Komlan Midodzi", "Noukpoape", email = "noukpoape@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Clusters sparse longitudinal trajectories with a mixture of
    linear mixed models whose mean curves are penalised B-splines
    (O'Sullivan penalty, smoothing parameter estimated by Fellner-Schall
    updates), optionally with covariates having cluster-specific effects
    and covariate-dependent cluster proportions. A greedy merge tree based
    on the exact integrated completed likelihood initialises an EM
    algorithm accelerated by SQUAREM, and the number of clusters is
    selected by BIC or ICL, or fixed by the user. Conjugate
    inverse-Wishart and inverse-gamma priors on the variance structure are
    calibrated from the empirical variogram of the residuals (Diggle,
    1988).
